2026-09-12T06:06Z claude note Review round on the 0686 item (1) patch. Two things land here. (1) The body gained the Relevant files, Test and Verification sections the handoff template asks for -- this ticket is a cold handoff and was missing three of them. (2) verification/probes/sdt-sitter-harness/bootstrap.js asserted `body.firstElementChild.id === 'sdt-global-section'`, stale since 0693's rendering put the switch row first (tests/sdt_sitter_dialog.mjs pins the order); Action 1 would have failed on it in a real window before reading anything it is there for. Corrected in the same commit, headless-unverifiable by construction -- the probe runs only in a real window -- so the order it now asserts is the one the dialog test pins.

2026-09-14T12:29Z claude note Orca pass DONE and recorded in verification/SDT-SITTER-UI-PANEL.md, speech quoted from Orca's own debug log. Orca speaks the toolbar control, the window, the switch, the coverage sentence and the end-of-work notice, all with correct roles and names. It found two defects nothing headless could: 0789 (the live region misses the switch-off transition -- asymmetric, and invisible on screen because the visible row is right in both directions) and 0790 (the toggle announces the next action, so a listener hears the opposite of what just happened -- found by the author listening, not by any instrument). Both filed, both Blocked-by this ticket, both under fix. Exit criteria rewritten on the author's instruction: the original set assumed the answer would be yes, and criterion 3 asked to delete a limitation that 0787 has since proved true.

