--- body ---
## Context

Parent: ticket 0686, item (2) of its 2026-09-08 entries. The supervision-panel
review's verdict was "CHANGES REQUESTED pour qualifier l'UI d'accessible". The
DOM/style smoke and the headless scenarios in `tests/sdt_sitter_bootstrap.mjs`
do not establish keyboard or screen-reader behaviour; only a real Zotero window
does. Ruled out of 0764's release gate on 2026-09-11 — see DECISIONS.md.

## Actions

1. Keyboard and focus, automatable: drive a real Zotero window through the RDP
   client of ticket 0766 (`bench/zotero_rdp_client.py`), synthesize key events
   in chrome context (`windowUtils`, as Mozilla's own `synthesizeKey` does),
   and run the assertions already carried by
   `verification/probes/sdt-sitter-harness/`: open the dialog from the
   keyboard, initial focus, each disclosure summary reachable, Escape closes,
   focus returns to the toolbar button. Against 0693's CURRENT layout.
2. Screen reader, manual: one Orca pass on Linux confirming the toolbar's
   accessible name and the transition announcements of 0686 item (1).

## Relevant files

- `verification/probes/sdt-sitter-harness/bootstrap.js` — the assertions to run;
  they exist and are unrun in a real window, which is this ticket's whole work
- `bench/zotero_rdp_client.py` — ticket 0766's client, the gesture driver
- `plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js` — `openDialog`, the focus order under test,
  and `announceSDTTransition`, whose utterances Orca must be heard to speak
- `tests/sdt_sitter_dialog.mjs` — the headless layout pin the probe must agree
  with; check it before trusting a probe assertion about layer order
- `verification/SDT-SITTER-UI-PANEL.md` — where the reading is recorded
- `plugins/sdt-sitter/RELEASE-NOTES.md` — carries the known-limitation line this
  ticket removes

## Test

Red step first, in a real window: run the harness probe unchanged and watch a
deliberate break go red — comment out the `keydown` listener that closes on
Escape, confirm the probe reports it, restore it. A probe that has never been
seen red in a real window has not been shown to be running there at all, which
is the failure mode this ticket exists to close (the stale layer-order anchor
corrected on 2026-09-12 is the same trap, caught by reading rather than running).

## Verification

- [ ] The probe runs in a real Zotero window and reports pass/fail per assertion.
- [ ] Each assertion has been seen red once, from a deliberate break, then green.
- [ ] The Orca pass names the Zotero and Orca versions and the announcements
      actually heard, quoted.

## Invariants

- The RDP client may perform the gestures but, per 0727's out-of-band
  condition, its own readings are not the verdict: the harness assertions are.

## Exit criteria

REWRITTEN 2026-09-14, on the author's instruction, because the original set was
written on the assumption that the answer would be "it works". Two of the three
could not be met by doing the work — only by the work coming out differently.

- [x] The panel's keyboard behaviour read in a real window, each assertion shown
      red once where a break could express it. `verification/probes/` carries the
      probe and the driver; the Escape assertion was red-armed, focus-return was
      not, and that is recorded rather than glossed.
- [x] Orca pass recorded in `verification/SDT-SITTER-UI-PANEL.md`, with speech
      quoted from Orca's own debug log rather than recalled.
- [x] `RELEASE-NOTES.md` states what a user actually gets. NOT the original
      criterion, which was to DELETE the limitation: ticket 0787 established the
      toolbar control is not reachable by Tab, so the limitation is true and
      stays. The notes now say so in the author's own words, and say what to do
      about it (click the button).

What the pass found is filed rather than fixed here: 0789 (the live region
misses the switch-off transition) and 0790 (the toggle announces the next
action). Both are `Blocked-by` this ticket, and both are being fixed under
their own numbers. Closing this one records that the reading was taken.
